(i) #{a1 a2 + b1 b2 = n, positive} = sum_{m<n} d(m) d(n-m) for 2 <= n <= 120 (brute force): True
(ii) ratio D(n) / ((6/pi^2) sigma(n) ln^2 n) on windows of 400 consecutive n; Ingham's error term is O(sigma(n) ln n ln ln n),
     i.e. the ratio is 1 + O(ln ln n / ln n)
   n in [20000, 20400): mean 1.0609, min 0.6963, max 1.2358, sd 0.1146; ln ln n / ln n = 0.232; corr(D(n)/n, sigma(n)/n) = 0.9788; odd n only: mean 1.1293, sd 0.0891
   n in [200000, 200400): mean 1.0507, min 0.7721, max 1.1953, sd 0.0952; ln ln n / ln n = 0.205; corr(D(n)/n, sigma(n)/n) = 0.9861; odd n only: mean 1.1070, sd 0.0739
   n in [1000000, 1000400): mean 1.0460, min 0.8082, max 1.1742, sd 0.0852; ln ln n / ln n = 0.190; corr(D(n)/n, sigma(n)/n) = 0.9893; odd n only: mean 1.0961, sd 0.0655
constants: 6/pi^2 = 0.6079271019 = 1/zeta(2);  (6/pi^2)/(1 - 1/4) = 0.8105694691;  8/pi^2 = 0.8105694691
